          "date": "2026-11-07 08:03:26.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-16507 lmv: refresh the statfs of every NOCREATE MDT",
        "message": "LU-16507 lmv: refresh the statfs of every NOCREATE MDT\n\nThe QoS and round-robin mkdir allocators skip an MDT marked NOCREATE,\nand lmv_locate_tgt_by_space() only refreshed the statfs of the parent\nMDT and of the MDT it picked.  Once no_create was cleared on another\nMDT, the client would keep avoiding that MDT for new directories until\nsomething else, like \"lfs df\", refreshed its statfs.  sanity test_413a\ncould fail with all directories on MDT0000 when it ran right after\ntest_413Aa, which marks every MDT NOCREATE.\n\nCheck every active MDT marked NOCREATE in lmv_locate_tgt_by_space(),\nthose other than the parent MDT only every 4 * qos_maxage, since\nNOCREATE is usually set for a long time.  Record when the async\nrequest is sent, and send no other request to the MDT for 2 seconds,\nrather than one more for each mkdir until the reply arrives.  The\nstatfs age still says when the last reply arrived.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nTest-Parameters: mdscount=2 mdtcount=4 testlist=conf-sanity env=ONLY=112b,ONLY_REPEAT=10\nFixes: 1dbcd0bab881 (\"LU-12998 mds: add no_create parameter to stop creates\")\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5.5 ltvm,llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I603b2c6c2cdcc400b7dd29a533267a37cc3ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
